---
intent: >
  Remove the `commands/aide/init` entry from the `COMMANDS` registry in
  `scaffoldCommands/index.ts` (and the matching entry from the upstream
  `initContent` `DOC_PATHS` registry it depends on), refresh the
  `scaffoldCommands/.aide` body sections so the count and enumerations
  match the post-deletion registry without pinning a specific size, and
  update the test file to assert against the new roster while honoring
  the spec's "no-count-pinning" undesired outcome.
---

## Project Structure

This plan governs only the `src/tools/init/scaffoldCommands/` module.
After execution, the `COMMANDS` array in `index.ts` has twelve entries
(orchestrator + eleven subcommands), the `.aide` body sections describe
the new roster without enumerating it inline as a fixed list, and the
test file asserts against the twelve-entry roster while removing
literal-count assertions where the spec's `outcomes.undesired` line
"a spec, test, description, or assertion that pins a specific count of
slash commands or enumerates the canonical command roster as part of
the contract" makes them anti-patterns.

```
src/tools/init/scaffoldCommands/
├── .aide                    ← (MODIFY) intent spec — frontmatter is already updated;
│                              this plan refreshes the body sections (## Context,
│                              ## Strategy, ## Good examples, ## Bad examples) so
│                              they no longer enumerate "13 entries" / "12 subcommands"
│                              / lifecycle-commands lists that include `init`
├── plan.aide                ← THIS plan (new)
├── todo.aide                ← prior QA artifact (already present; do not touch)
├── index.ts                 ← (MODIFY) export default async function scaffoldCommands(
│                              commandDir: string): Promise<InitStep[]>. The COMMANDS
│                              registry shrinks from thirteen to twelve entries —
│                              the `{ canonical: "commands/aide/init", hostPath:
│                              "aide/init.md", displayName: "aide:init" }` entry is
│                              removed. Function signature, JSDoc, and the
│                              for-loop body are unchanged.
└── index.test.ts            ← (MODIFY) Vitest suite. Updates the roster assertion
                                in the cold-run test to twelve entries (still using
                                an array equality so the canonical order stays
                                pinned) and removes the literal length assertion
                                `expect(results).toHaveLength(13)` from places
                                where it pins a count for its own sake. The
                                roster-equality assertion in the cold-run test
                                continues to enforce both membership AND order.
```

The `.aide` body sections that change are listed for the implementor's
benefit:

- **`## Context`** — currently mentions "the canonical docs" without an
  inline count; verify it stays count-free after re-read. No edit
  expected unless the body has drifted.
- **`## Strategy`** — contains the literal "iterates over a fixed
  COMMANDS registry of 13 entries: the orchestrator (`aide.md` at the
  command directory root) plus 12 subcommands under `aide/` — the seven
  pipeline phases (research, spec, synthesize, plan, build, qa, fix),
  three lifecycle commands (upgrade, init, align), and two maintenance
  commands (update-playbook, refactor)". This is the largest rewrite —
  the prose must describe the registry's SHAPE without enumerating its
  membership. It also includes "for example 'aide: created, research:
  created, spec: exists, synthesize: created, plan: created, build:
  created, qa: created, fix: exists, upgrade: created, init: created,
  update-playbook: created, refactor: created, align: created'" — the
  example status line that lists `init: created` in the middle.
- **`## Good examples`** — contains "writes `aide.md` at the command
  directory root (the orchestrator) and 12 subcommand files into
  `.claude/commands/aide/` (or the equivalent for the detected
  framework) — all 13 entries in the COMMANDS registry — and returns
  a `created` status for each", and another sentence "The other 12
  commands also report `exists`." Both must be re-cast as
  count-free descriptions.
- **`## Bad examples`** — verify this section does NOT pin a count
  after re-read; the existing bad examples mostly describe failure
  shapes, not membership. No edit expected unless the body has drifted.

## Prerequisites

This plan modifies the upstream `initContent` `DOC_PATHS` registry as
part of step 1, because the `commands/aide/init` canonical name in
`DOC_PATHS` is what `scaffoldCommands.COMMANDS` looked up. Both
registries must change in the same logical unit of work — leaving one
without the other produces either:

- A `COMMANDS` entry referencing a `canonical` name no longer in
  `DOC_PATHS` (TypeScript compile error: the `CanonicalDocName` type
  union loses the `"commands/aide/init"` literal, and the `COMMANDS`
  entry's `canonical` field becomes invalid), or
- A `DOC_PATHS` entry pointing at a deleted file (runtime throw on
  `readCanonicalDoc("commands/aide/init")` if anything still calls
  it).

Both edits land in the same step (step 1) so the plan is internally
self-contained. There are no external prerequisite modules.

